red valuable insights beyond the official information. He showed us the best quiet study spots in the library, which cafes offer student discounts, and even which professors are known for particularly challenging assessments. The tour ended at the Student Centre, where various clubs and societies had set up information booths. The diversity of options was impressive\u2014everything from sports and academic societies to cultural and special interest groups. I signed up for the Indian Society, the Computing Society, and the Hiking Club, hoping these will provide both professional networking and social opportunities. In the evening, there was a welcome reception with refreshments, where I had longer conversations with some of the people I'd met earlier. Elena and I discovered we're both interested in machine learning applications, while Ibrahim has professional experience in software development that he's eager to build upon. Lin seemed quieter but opened up when discussing our shared anxiety about the workload ahead. As we talked about our backgrounds and aspirations, I felt a sense of connection forming. These might be the people who become my closest friends here, or at least my academic support network. Walking back to my apartment, I reflected on how quickly life can change. Just four days ago, I was saying goodbye to my family at Mumbai Airport, and now I'm forming new connections halfway across the world. The homesickness is still there, a dull ache beneath the excitement, but today helped me see the possibilities this year holds. The academic challenges will be significant\u2014I'm under no illusions about that\u2014but having met others on the same journey makes it seem more manageable. Tomorrow is the Computer Science program-specific orientation, which should provide more details about our modules, assessments, and faculty. I'm particularly keen to learn about research opportunities and industry connections, as gaining practical experience will be crucial for my post-graduation plans.", "response": "{\n  \"sentiment_score\": 0.8,\n  \"emotion_tags\": [\"excited\", \"hopeful\", \"connected\", \"nervous\", \"curious\"]\n}", "metadata": {"assistant_id": "asst_jm7SRfvBX5919YJMudt5r5vk", "thread_id": "thread_oy4jBrQJJccQ7DSxAppTNlhO", "used_tools": false}}
